name o4-06-merge-1
timeout 300

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 6 OF 10 — THE MERGE, and the half of the campaign the anchor is famous for.
# doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md mission 6. Same file as o4-04-entry-10nm.fbm with the entries at
# 2.00 nm and fresh callsigns, for the same reason o4-05 has them.
#
# THE SPEC LISTED THIS MISSION AS BLOCKED, AND IT IS NOT BLOCKED ANY MORE. When O4 was written the
# merge could not be read: duel-merge.fbm ran its full 300 s with no K.O. on either side, a 24-round
# GSh-301 burst that missed, and 220.1 s of the run with BOTH jets' bfm_rng at -1 — neither ACM box
# re-acquires after the first pass (doc/pilot.md 2.9). Four control-law blockers have closed since (the
# MiG's close-combat departure, its acquisition, the F-16's roll law, the MiG's missing rate damper) and
# the fifth closed on 2026-07-29: Phase::Bfm ended its tick in BfmGunfire and the round on the rail had
# no employment path at all (doc/pilot.md 5.11). duel-merge went exit 3 -> 0 and duel-merge-stern
# exit 0. The re-acquisition gap is still open and it no longer BLOCKS this mission, because the fight
# is decided on the first pass and there is no second pass to acquire for.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: with both jets inside every launch envelope either side owns from the first
# tick, what decides — and is it the thing the quotation names? The quotation names three: the IRST, the
# helmet sight and the Archer. Two of the three are modelled and reach this fight (the R-73's own cueing
# limit is the BFM_SHOT gate's cueDeg 60 against the AIM-9's 30); the third is published to a block
# nobody reads (doc/duels.md D3), and o4-08-weather.fbm measures exactly what that costs.
#
# WHAT THE TREE ALREADY KNOWS ABOUT THIS CELL, so this file is read against it and not in a vacuum:
# on the head-on merge the F-16 wins 30 of 30 arena runs (doc/doctrine-evolution.md E4 §1, `xmerge`),
# because it spawns in ACM HUD while the MiG must switch its N019 over the bus — worth 1.9 s against
# 1.5 — and because the AIM-9M's 9.4 kg warhead kills this airframe inside 2.32 m where the R-73's
# 7.4 kg needs 2.08 m. This file removes the first of those two: the MiG is briefed into ACM from the
# spawn, exactly as o4-04 and o4-05 are. What is left is the warhead and the arrival geometry.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29): exit 0, THE F-16 WINS, and the MiG still shot first. Shots at t=1.5 (2,968 m)
# and t=1.9 (2,773 m); the R-73 arrives 2.608 m out against its own 2.08 m kill radius and DEGRADES, the
# AIM-9 arrives 1.396 m out against 2.32 m and KILLS at t=6.5. Neither the cueing envelope nor the gun
# decides the knife fight — the WARHEAD does, 9.4 kg against 7.4, and 0.4 s of shot lead does not close
# it. Read beside o4-04 (MiG at 10 nm) and o4-05 (trade at 5 nm): the anchor's claim holds at its own
# outer edge and fails at the inner one.
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-07-29 after the spawn-tick frame fix (doc/sensors.md 10, item 24): exit 0 -> 1, the
# TRADE this file's own reading rule already names. The two shots are unchanged in time and range
# (t = 0.8 / 1.0, 3,309 / 3,211 m). What moved is 1 m of arrival: the R-73 now arrives 1.646 m out
# INSIDE its own 2.08 m kill radius instead of 2.608 m outside it, and the AIM-9 2.067 m inside its
# 2.32 m. Both kill, 0.1 s apart. THE WARHEAD CLAIM ABOVE IS THEREFORE WITHDRAWN AS MEASURED HERE: at
# 380 kt head-on inside 3.5 km this arena decides nothing, because both rounds arrive inside both kill
# radii and which K.O. is declared first is which round was fired first minus its time of flight. A
# campaign that wants the warhead priced needs a geometry where only one round arrives.
#
# READING RULE: the verdict is the TELEMETRY. Read the two BFM_SHOT times, then the DETONATION missM
# against each round's own fuze radius, then the damage KILL lines. exit 0 = one side decided it,
# exit 1 = a TRADE (both dead; doc/missions/verdict.md refuses to invent a winner and reports the first
# unit's FAIL), exit 3 = neither round arrived. exit 2 would be a defect.

unit viper4
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 13.57090 5000 90.0 380       # 2.00 nm apart: a genuine merge
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9                            # firing order: the infrared rounds first
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 5000 380               # hulkeast: the MiG's own range target
  objective kill unit fulcrum4
  objective survive

unit fulcrum4
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.20000 13.62910 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode acm                           # briefed INTO the fight: the close-combat auto-lock volume
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set kols_mode ir_cc                         # the KOLS in its close-combat field — the third of the
  set kols_laser on                           # quotation's three reasons, and the one o4-08 can blind
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 55.20000 12.60000 5000 380               # hulkwest: the F-16's own range target
  objective kill unit viper4
  objective survive

unit hulkwest
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 55.20000 12.60000 ground 90.0 0

unit hulkeast
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 55.20000 14.60000 ground 270.0 0
